1.1 Case Study Description: Federal University of Technology, Owerri (FUTO) Result Portal
Context & Business Scenario
The Federal University of Technology, Owerri (FUTO) is a public university operating multiple specialized academic schools, such as the School of Engineering and Engineering Technology (SEET), the School of Information and Communications Technology (SICT), and a lot more Schools as can be noted. 
The FUTO Student Result Portal manages the end-to-end academic lifecycle for over 30,000 active students across undergraduate and postgraduate programmes.

System Users
 * Students: View registered courses, check semester results, compute CGPA, and generate transcripts.

 * Lecturers (Course Advisors / Examiners): Upload raw continuous assessment (CA) and examination marks for assigned courses.

*  Heads of Department (HODs) / Deans of Schools: Review, approve, or reject submitted departmental grade sheets.

*  Exams & Records Officers: Audit final grades, approve transcript requests, and process academic standing (e.g., First Class, Probation).

*  System Administrators: Manage user access control, database security, and audit logs.

Core System Operations
* Course registration and unit validation during semester enrollment.

* Multi-tier grade entry, calculation, approval, and publication.

* Dynamic calculation of Semester Grade Point Average (SGPA) and Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) based on FUTO's 5.0 grading scale.

* Immutable audit logging for grade modifications.

